- [x] Unix socket support (POSIX; "unix:/path" in any host string with ConnectionType::TCP, ports ignored, stale socket files taken over on bind)
- [x] Limit array/vector/string read sizes (ZNET_MAX_READ_ELEMENTS / ZNET_MAX_READ_STRING_LENGTH, plus a bytes-on-hand check that needs no configuration)
- [x] Connection throttling (IP / CIDR) (ServerOptions::max_attempts_per_source / attempt_window; per-source window at TCP accept and ZDT first contact, bounded table that fails open. The rendezvous server exposes ServerOptions too and adds a per-client request limit with idempotent identify.)
- [x] Option to dump the received buffer when a packet fails to decode (CommonOptions::dump_on_decode_failure, capped at 512 bytes)
- [x] Option to close the connection on invalid received packets (CommonOptions::max_invalid_frames, default 16, zero disables; counted per session and surfaced as the invalid_frames metric)
- [x] Max concurrent connections (ZDT: config max_connections + NoFreeConnections)
- [x] Peer to peer TCP hole-punching (also UDP/ZDT via PunchSyncZDT)
- [x] Validate IP addresses
- [x] Public key authentication (ExportKeyingMaterial is the library primitive; examples/auth shows the full pattern with service-signed tokens and a session-bound client signature. Identity policy stays with the application.)
- [x] Allowlists and denylists (ServerOptions::allowlist / denylist of CIDRBlocks; deny wins, ZDT refuses silently, v4 rules catch v4-mapped v6 sources)
- [x] Idle timeout and ping-pong (CommonOptions::idle_timeout / keepalive_interval drive both transports; ZDT had it, TCP gained zero-length control frames for ping/pong)
- [x] Abstract transport
- [x] Mock transport (tests/session_pair.h: FakeTransport plus a two-session Pair harness over a hand-pumped wire)
- [ ] Fuzz testing
